**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.astro

.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.DS_Store
*.log

# Not part of the site build.
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yaml
deploy_docker.sh
.dockerignore
README.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# `.env` is deliberately NOT ignored: Astro reads the PUBLIC_* values from it
# at build time and bakes them into the HTML, so the build stage needs it.
#
# It is not exposed by doing so. The build is multi-stage and the final image
# copies only `dist/` across, so `.env` is in neither the served image nor the
# nginx web root, and it cannot be requested over HTTP. Every value in it is
# public by definition, since it ends up in the HTML either way.
#
# The rule that follows: never put a real secret in this file. Anything secret
# belongs in a build argument or a Docker secret instead.
